<p class="kicker">Capabilities · manifest {{ webmcp.manifest.manifest_version }} · tools {{ webmcp.manifest.tools_version }}</p>
<h1>For AI agents</h1>
<p class="lede">Use any agent you like. The same {{ webmcp.manifest.capabilities.length }} capabilities are available through several interfaces, so nothing ties you to one AI provider, browser or hosted service.</p>

<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>What these tools can't do:</strong> post, publish, sign in, change infrastructure, or certify anything. Every capability is read-only or prepare-only. Drafts, PR descriptions and AT Protocol records are returned to you to review and submit yourself. No tool runs code from a repository, and only the repository-assessment tools (and an assessment record built from a live scan) fetch anything: public files from GitHub, with no credentials.</p>
</div>

<h2>Interfaces</h2>
<dl>
{%- for k, v in webmcp.manifest.interfaces %}
  <dt><strong>{{ k }}</strong></dt><dd>{{ v }}</dd>
{%- endfor %}
</dl>

<h3 id="mcp">Use the local MCP server</h3>
<p>Any MCP client can start it. It reads this repository's files, so it works offline and without jollyrogercharter.org:</p>
<pre><code>git clone {{ repoUrl }}.git jrc
# in your MCP client's server configuration:
{ "command": "node", "args": ["/path/to/jrc/bin/jrc-mcp.mjs"] }</code></pre>
<h3 id="cli">Use the CLI</h3>
<pre><code>node bin/jrc.mjs tool list
echo '{"skills":["writing"]}' | node bin/jrc.mjs tool find_opportunities --input -</code></pre>
<h3 id="webmcp">Use WebMCP</h3>
<p>Open this site in a browser with WebMCP enabled; the tools register on every page. Native registration hasn't been verified yet. See the <a href="{% sourceLink "docs/WEBMCP.md" %}">developer guide</a>.</p>
<h3 id="assess-a-repository">Assess a repository</h3>
<p><code>assess_repository</code> reads a public GitHub repository's file list and a few key files at one commit. An automated scan isn't a review: <em>missing</em> means not found, not proof of noncompliance. The <a href="/adopt/">adoption page</a> runs the same code.</p>

<h2>All capabilities</h2>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Capabilities by interface"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Every capability and the interfaces that support it</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Safety</th><th scope="col">WebMCP / MCP</th><th scope="col">HTTP</th><th scope="col">CLI</th><th scope="col">Page</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for c in webmcp.manifest.capabilities %}
    <tr><th scope="row"><code>{{ c.name }}</code><br>{{ c.title }}</th><td>{{ c.group }}{% if c.maturity != "implemented" %}<br><small>{{ c.maturity }}</small>{% endif %}</td><td>{{ c.safety }}{% if c.network != "none" %}<br><small>network: {{ c.network }}</small>{% endif %}</td><td>yes</td><td>{% if c.interfaces.http_static %}<a href="{{ c.interfaces.http_static }}"><code>{{ c.interfaces.http_static }}</code></a>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td><td>{% if c.interfaces.cli %}<code>{{ c.interfaces.cli }}</code>{% else %}<code>jrc tool {{ c.name }}</code>{% endif %}</td><td>{% if c.interfaces.website %}<a href="{{ c.interfaces.website }}">{{ c.interfaces.website }}</a>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Machine-readable: <a href="/api/v1/capabilities.json"><code>/api/v1/capabilities.json</code></a> (schemas, annotations, safety, maturity, interfaces) and <a href="/api/v1/tools.json"><code>/api/v1/tools.json</code></a>.</p>

